insert into public.lessons (topic_id, objectives, explanation, code_lang, code, code_explanation, activity, mistakes, recap, version) select id, '["Explain introduction to css in your own words.","Recognise and apply: CSS controls layout, colour, spacing and typography.","Recognise and apply: an external stylesheet keeps styling separate from HTML.","Complete the practical activity and check it against the success criteria."]'::jsonb, '["This lesson covers introduction to css: what CSS does, how to attach it, and the cascade. It is written for a complete beginner, so every idea is introduced in plain language before any code appears.","The first key idea is that CSS controls layout, colour, spacing and typography. In practice that means a learner should be able to recognise it in a real page or project, not only repeat a definition. Work through the example below slowly and predict what each line does before reading its explanation.","The second key idea is that an external stylesheet keeps styling separate from HTML. This is the idea most beginners get wrong, so the common-mistakes section below shows the wrong version next to the corrected version.","Finally, remember that how introduction to css fits into real web development work. A professional developer does not memorise every detail — they understand the idea, practise it on a small real task, and check their work. That is exactly what the practical activity at the end of this lesson asks you to do."]'::jsonb, 'css', '/* styles.css — one file styles every page that links it */
