insert into public.lessons (topic_id, objectives, explanation, code_lang, code, code_explanation, activity, mistakes, recap, version) select id, '["Explain debugging and error handling in your own words.","Recognise and apply: read the error message first: file, line and type point at the cause.","Recognise and apply: an error boundary catches render errors so one broken component cannot blank the app.","Complete the practical activity and check it against the success criteria."]'::jsonb, '["This lesson covers debugging and error handling: finding and fixing bugs with devtools, logs and error boundaries. It is written for a complete beginner, so every idea is introduced in plain language before any code appears.","The first key idea is that read the error message first: file, line and type point at the cause. In practice that means a learner should be able to recognise it in a real page or project, not only repeat a definition. Work through the example below slowly and predict what each line does before reading its explanation.","The second key idea is that an error boundary catches render errors so one broken component cannot blank the app. This is the idea most beginners get wrong, so the common-mistakes section below shows the wrong version next to the corrected version.","Finally, remember that how debugging and error handling fits into real web development work. A professional developer does not memorise every detail — they understand the idea, practise it on a small real task, and check their work. That is exactly what the practical activity at the end of this lesson asks you to do."]'::jsonb, 'javascript', 'try {
