insert into public.lessons (topic_id, objectives, explanation, code_lang, code, code_explanation, activity, mistakes, recap, version) select id, '["Explain rest api development in your own words.","Recognise and apply: GET reads, POST creates, PUT/PATCH updates, DELETE removes.","Recognise and apply: use 400 for bad input, 401 for unauthenticated, 403 for forbidden, 404 for missing.","Complete the practical activity and check it against the success criteria."]'::jsonb, '["This lesson covers rest api development: designing REST endpoints: resources, methods, status codes and validation. It is written for a complete beginner, so every idea is introduced in plain language before any code appears.","The first key idea is that GET reads, POST creates, PUT/PATCH updates, DELETE removes. In practice that means a learner should be able to recognise it in a real page or project, not only repeat a definition. Work through the example below slowly and predict what each line does before reading its explanation.","The second key idea is that use 400 for bad input, 401 for unauthenticated, 403 for forbidden, 404 for missing. This is the idea most beginners get wrong, so the common-mistakes section below shows the wrong version next to the corrected version.","Finally, remember that how rest api development fits into real web development work. A professional developer does not memorise every detail — they understand the idea, practise it on a small real task, and check their work. That is exactly what the practical activity at the end of this lesson asks you to do."]'::jsonb, 'typescript', 'export async function POST(req: Request) {
